  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+3x+3 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x-3}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x.$",
